Hi,

Four fixes for the single-queue ibmveth driver. None depends on the
multi-queue RX series. Three can take the networking stack down with
no recovery short of a reboot.

They target net-next rather than net: the triggers are rare (an
open() failure during a direct reopen, PHYP returning a bad
correlator, netconsole under TX contention) and there are no field
reports. They also go ahead of the multi-queue RX series, which
builds on them. Each carries a Fixes: tag for stable selection.

Patch 1 removes ndo_poll_controller. It ran replenish from netpoll
outside NAPI with no lock, racing NAPI's replenish on the same pool:
a free slot could be posted to PHYP twice (memory corruption). The
trigger is narrow (netconsole plus TX lock contention), but the
callback is unnecessary since netpoll polls NAPI itself, as was done
for ibmvnic.

  Fixes: 6b4223748895 ("[PATCH] ibmveth: Add netpoll function")

Patch 2 stops a second close() after a failed direct reopen.
change_mtu, the pool sysfs store, set_csum and set_tso close and
reopen the device directly; if that open() fails, IFF_UP stays set
and the next ndo_stop napi_disable()s an already-disabled NAPI with
RTNL held. The hang is deterministic once open() has failed (for
example on an MTU change under memory pressure), and it also blocks
shutdown.

  Fixes: 860f242eb534 ("[PATCH] ibmveth change buffer pools dynamically")

Patch 3 makes poll step past a bad RX slot. Since 2c91e2319ed9
turned the correlator BUG_ON()s into WARN_ON() plus a reset, poll
breaks out without advancing the ring and restarts on the same slot
forever, and the reset meant to recover deadlocks in napi_disable()
against that loop. The WARN_ON()s on PHYP-supplied data become a
ratelimited error.

  Fixes: 2c91e2319ed9 ("net: ibmveth: Reset the adapter when unexpected states are detected")

Patch 4 rejects correlators that name an inactive buffer pool, which
passed the size check and dereferenced a NULL skbuff array in
softirq.

  Fixes: 860f242eb534 ("[PATCH] ibmveth change buffer pools dynamically")

Patches 2-4 answer review comments on v7 of the multi-queue RX
series, which asked for exactly these to be split out with Fixes:
tags so stable can take them without the MQ refactor
(https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/cover.1790319558.git.mmc@linux.ibm.com/).
Patch 1 came out of the follow-up review of the same code.

Taking them first also simplifies that series. With
ndo_poll_controller gone, napi_disable() alone fences netpoll, so
queue resize no longer needs netpoll_poll_disable() on its error
paths or a closed-state guard in the callback. The opened gate and
the bad-slot handling become existing behaviour that the MQ patches
extend per queue, instead of fixes buried in feature patches.

Testing:
* ibmveth KUnit suite on qemu pseries (ppc64le): 3/3 pass. The two
  new cases fail on the unfixed driver: harvest leaves the ring
  index unchanged, and the inactive-pool correlator oopses with a
  NULL dereference.
* ppc64le W=1 build of each patch, with and without the KUnit code;
  no warnings. checkpatch --strict clean.

